P2 — Detail promo badge can survive an empty departure selection.

Location: [StructuredPages.tsx:1346](/E:/repo/WingsTravel/app/src/tours/StructuredPages.tsx:1346), using the fallback at [StructuredPages.tsx:1065](/E:/repo/WingsTravel/app/src/tours/StructuredPages.tsx:1065).

Evidence: Before explicitly clicking a departure, choose a city/month combination with no matching departure. The provider clears `selectedDeparture` at [TourDepartureSelectionContext.tsx:187](/E:/repo/WingsTravel/app/src/tours/TourDepartureSelectionContext.tsx:187), leaving `isSelectionExplicit` false. The header therefore falls back to `nextDepartureProp` and retains its promotion badge. The price rail instead uses the null selection and displays “Contact”/“Liên hệ”. Badge and price no longer describe the same selection.

Minimal fix: Make the header respect a null selection from the provider, matching the rail. Add a regression covering incompatible city/month filters with an initially promoted departure. The fallback predates this delta; displaying its stale promotion badge is introduced here.

Other checks:

- `git rev-parse HEAD` returned `58633ae36834bcc0869237f5565d12ccac41929d`; ancestry check exited 0.
- `git diff --exit-code HEAD -- app/src/collections/TourDepartures.ts` exited 0. Promotion fields already exist; this visual delta requires no schema migration. Other pending migrations remain outside scope.
- Normalized DTO paths retain departure identity and suppress ineligible discounts. Original `<del>` precedes the red discounted price.
- Existing locale issue outside this delta: catalog callers omit locale, and contact cards render the Vietnamese DTO label.
- The initial Server/Client helper issue was removed concurrently during review; it is not an outstanding finding in the latest files read.

No builds, application tests, ARM64 checks, or desktop/mobile browser checks were run; clipping and overflow remain unverified. No files were edited, and no secrets or production commands were accessed.
